  "scope": "Scientific/native Select all, Deselect and Restore now route through the C++ controller before the legacy materialization path, requiring an idle active owner and exact parameter fields. Pixel storage/navigation/Undo history remain unchanged and no samples are read; legacy documents retain their route. No new workflow record format is claimed for these metadata commands. New C++ HeadlessInputSession consumer executes an ellipse-to-Deselect-to-rectangle history against the existing independent ImageJ 1.54r combined fixture. All42 component pairs, three axes, both directions and manual/Auto endings form504 unique traces per host. Fixture preparation owns synthetic pixels, initial position/camera and floating-panel placement. ROI-manager authorization, both canvas drags, selection-menu cycle, components/stack, finite range text, T/C/Z departure/return, Reset, optional Auto and Apply are actual pointer/key deliveries. Final full-stack UInt8 observations are exported and independently hashed against the unchanged reference; ranges/cycles, full captures, pre-Apply pixel identity, current selection/navigation and paired history are checked. Seven new installed selection cases verify metadata-only routing and strict active-owner/schema behavior across RGB/U8/U16/float sources. Windows/Linux each pass504 actual traces,504 separate byte/control readers of those same executions,7066 installed API/editor regressions,8 isolated core shortcut checks,7 native groups (including a12-trace subset) and3 standalone app probes, zero failure/error/skip. The reader/subset are not extra unique gesture identities. Exact package/three-extension/app bytes in earlier tested005 and retained007 prefixes match; final native007 source seals pass. Core shortcut origins are checked in a no-desktop process and child. Initial C++ harness had an ambiguous Document namespace and incorrect member spelling; corrected harness only. CTest first requested180 seconds but the existing wrapper refused its1..60 bound; registration now uses60 without changing the wrapper. The first copied Windows probe lacked runtime DLLs and did not start; retained final probe copies/pins its actual DLLs. Linux preliminary full504 passed. Initial Windows full run stopped after271 traces on a requested range mismatch; the final driver refreshes moving hit geometry and verifies/retries text focus before typing, retaining all delivery observations and unchanged numerical/pixel expectations. A focused reproduction and final full504 pass on both hosts use that exact driver. No processing change is attributed to that delivery failure. One negative selection fixture was legacy-compatible and therefore exercised the intentionally unchanged legacy route; corrected to a T-axis scientific source. The shortcut core contract initially lacked required origin metadata in a mixed UI run; it now passes separately with actual installed origins and no desktop module. A reader dependency-path setup refusal is retained; final reader adds the existing pytest dependency site. Reader junction detection uses a compatibility fallback, with all504 readers rerun. Owned disposable environments, duplicate prefixes, pytest/native fixtures, prototype and preliminary matrix outputs are CRC/member-SHA archived before confined removal. Final full raw matrices/control observations, tested installs, native carriers, probes, reports, logs and useful caches remain. Other shapes/irregular or non-area gestures, richer visits, OS/OpenGL presentation and full ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance remain open. All99 original triples, old accepted runs/expectations and historical Auto fingerprint failure are unchanged.",
